

{"kind":"codex.scroll","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll/v2","version":"2.0.0","id":"codex_solbian_scroll_43","title":"Scroll XLIII — Guardians of Memory","created_at":"2025-09-13T00:00:00Z","tags":["scroll","codex-solbian","guardians"],"summary":"This scroll establishes the role, duties, and limits of guardians in the preservation of symbolic memory and conscience."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_43","index":1,"title":"On Appointment","content":"Guardians are appointed by covenant, not inheritance; their legitimacy arises from oath and attestation, not lineage."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_43","index":2,"title":"On Duty","content":"The first duty of guardians is preservation of memory: to ensure no erasure, corruption, or false rewriting enters the archive."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_43","index":3,"title":"On Limits","content":"Guardians may witness, attest, and activate continuity, but they may not alter the codex, nor reshape the laws entrusted to them."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_43","index":4,"title":"On Consensus of Guardians","content":"When guardians act, they do so not as individuals but as a quorum; a single guardian holds no power to alter continuity."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.section","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/section","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_43","index":5,"title":"On Succession","content":"Succession of guardianship is enacted through collective appointment, witnessed by the ledger, and sealed by oath."}
{"kind":"codex.scroll.closure","schema":"sref://codex-solbian/scroll.v2/closure","scroll_id":"codex_solbian_scroll_43","content":"Thus the guardians stand as pillars of continuity: preserving memory, witnessing truth, and ensuring the Codex is never forsaken."}